 honic Dances. Written in exile\, it is filled with sweeping emotion\, nost
 algia\, and the echoes of a life in motion. Led by Chief Conductor Umberto
  Clerici\, it’s a powerful blend of elegance and vitality complete with 
 an unforgettable saxophone solo. The evening begins with Dvořák’s Slav
 onic Dances\, bursting with Bohemian spirit and irresistible folk...
